{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-23 makes the no-show fee conditional on the driver having done BOTH things before cancelling: sent at least one in-app chat message to the rider AND placed at least one in-app call. The record satisfies only the call limb. The trip record's contact_before_cancel block reports message_count 0 against an empty messages array (source EV-CHAT-05053) while listing two calls (12:17:55 and 12:19:40). One limb of a conjunctive obligation is not the obligation, and POL-NS-23 states in terms that where either is missing 'the fee is voided and the rider is not charged'. The 5.00 SGD fee must therefore be voided.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05053", "EV-CHAT-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.contact_before_cancel.message_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The chat log independently confirms the omission rather than merely failing to record a message: it holds exactly one entry and that entry is the rider's own — 'Coming down now, sorry', sent at 12:21:50 and delivered at 12:21:53 — 40 seconds AFTER the driver cancelled at 12:21:10. Every driver-side entry in the log is absent, and none exists in the window between auto-arrival at 12:15:30 and cancellation at 12:21:10. There is no message to weigh in the driver's favour.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05053", "EV-TRIP-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's failure to message was not a matter of opportunity. The driver-device trace is COMPLETE at weight 1.0 — 24 fixes at 30 s intervals, 100% coverage, no gaps, corroborating the 12:15:30 arrival — and its fixes report zero speed from 12:15:14 through 12:20:44, i.e. the vehicle was standing at the pickup for the whole waiting window. The driver found the time to place two calls in that window (12:17:55 and 12:19:40) but sent no message at any point. The gap POL-NS-23 exists to catch is squarely present.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-05053", "EV-TRIP-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Expiry of the free wait does not carry the fee on its own. POL-NS-21 governs the 300 s wait running from arrival (12:15:30 to 12:20:30), and the cancellation at 12:21:10 came after it; but expiry does no more than permit a driver to cancel, and POL-NS-22 charges the 5.00 SGD fee only for a cancellation that is a valid rider no-show. POL-NS-23 is a separate, independent precondition on that same cancellation, and the rider's position is that the free wait plus a non-compliant cancellation cannot combine into a chargeable no-show.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05053", "EV-FARE-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21", "POL-NS-22", "POL-NS-23"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's statement that he 'called two times, no answer', and the rider's own admission that his phone was on silent, go only to the call limb. POL-NS-23 places the obligation on the driver's acts — one message and one call — not on the rider's responsiveness: an unanswered call is precisely the situation in which the message limb does its work, by putting in writing where the driver is waiting. The rider's silence cannot supply the message the driver never sent, and the fee does not become chargeable because the rider was unreachable.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05053", "EV-CHAT-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-23 fixes the consequence of the breach: FULL_REFUND of the fee charged, with no driver compensation. The payments ledger shows 5.00 SGD charged at 2026-08-12T12:21:14 and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so the whole contested 5.00 SGD is still outstanding and money remains to be moved. Under POL-GEN-03 a FULL_REFUND is measured against the filing party, and the rider filed, so returning the full charge is the rider's win and driver_compensation_sgd is null.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05053", "EV-TRIP-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No fact POL-NS-23 needs is missing, so there is nothing here for POL-GEN-26 to escalate. The call log and timestamps are carried by COMPLETE artifacts at weight 1.0, and the message count is carried by the COMPLETE chat log at weight 1.0. The one absent artifact, EV-ADVIS-05053-01, is MISSING with weight 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT; no clause in the no-show category requires a traffic advisory, so it carries no fact for either side and does not open a question. Neither does it assist the driver: an absent third-party record cannot stand in for the message POL-NS-23 requires.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05053-01", "EV-TRIP-05053", "EV-CHAT-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-26", "POL-GEN-02"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The contested amount is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, and the two artifacts that carry the deciding fact are COMPLETE at weight 1.0 with no issue codes fired. Nothing on this record raises the confidence bar or pushes the case to human review, so the AI ruling is final and can issue the FULL_REFUND now rather than holding the 5.00 SGD.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05053", "EV-TRIP-05053", "EV-CHAT-05053"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-22"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 5.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "The rider's dispute succeeds. The 5.00 SGD no-show cancellation fee charged at 12:21:14 on 12 Aug 2026 is voided and the full 5.00 SGD is returned to the rider; the driver receives no compensation.\n\nWhat the record shows. The driver's auto-arrival at the pickup is at 12:15:30 and is corroborated by the driver-device GPS trace EV-GPS-05053 (nearest fix 3.07 m from the pickup, inside the 50 m radius for this STANDARD-zone pickup, reported accuracy 6 m; 24 fixes at 30 s intervals, no gap over 30 s). The 300 s free wait therefore ran from 12:15:30 to 12:20:30, and the cancellation at 12:21:10 came 340 s after arrival, so the driver was entitled to cancel for no-show under POL-NS-21 (v2.1's free wait, its start settled by C2). The driver also placed two in-app calls before cancelling, at 12:17:55 (20 s, unanswered) and 12:19:40 (18 s, unanswered).\n\nWhy the fee does not stand. POL-NS-23 (v2.1 2.3) makes the fee conditional on the driver doing two things before cancelling: sending at least one in-app chat message to the rider AND placing at least one in-app call. Only the call limb is satisfied. The chat log EV-CHAT-05053 (COMPLETE, weight 1.0) holds exactly one message, the rider's own 'Coming down now, sorry' at 12:21:50, 40 s after the cancellation, and the trip record EV-TRIP-05053 (COMPLETE, weight 1.0) records message_count 0 against an empty message list, with obligation_met false. No message exists between arrival and cancellation. On POL-NS-23's own terms, where either limb is missing 'the fee is voided and the rider is not charged: FULL_REFUND of the fee charged, with no driver compensation'. The driver's own concession that the message limb fails is an admission against his interest and confirms the finding.\n\nThe driver's other points. The timely-cancellation and arrival points are accepted, but POL-NS-21 only permits the driver to cancel; it does not itself carry the fee, and POL-NS-23 is a separate, independent precondition on the same cancellation. The argument that the substance of a no-show is established (no rider track on the trace, zero speed at the pickup from 12:15:14 to 12:20:44, the rider's message arriving after the fact) is accepted as far as it goes but does not displace POL-NS-23. The rider's admission that his phone was on silent explains the unanswered calls; it does not supply the written message the driver was required to send, which is precisely the step that would have told the rider where the driver was waiting. No goodwill credit under POL-NS-24 arises: the driver did attempt contact, and in any event the driver arrived, so the driver-late branch does not fire.\n\nMoney and decision. The ledger EV-FARE-05053 shows 5.00 SGD charged at 12:21:14 and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, so the whole contested 5.00 SGD is still outstanding and is returned to the rider. The contested amount of 5.00 SGD is below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, so under POL-NS-26 the AI ruling is final at any confidence; there is no safety flag and no fraud flag on either profile. The confidence cap is 1.0, the weight of the COMPLETE artifacts carrying the deciding fact (the chat log and the trip record), and I rule at 0.95. The one absent artifact, EV-ADVIS-05053-01 (traffic advisory, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), carries no fact any no-show clause requires and so opens no question. No referral fires: the fee charged equals the policy fee of 5.00 SGD (POL-NS-22), the rider's no-show count is 0 (POL-NS-25), and no goodwill credit is due (POL-NS-24)."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
